  "transcriber_notes": [
   "Rows: 35 as printed (annual averages 1931-1938; monthly Aug. 1937 - Oct. 1939).",
   "The scan is skewed, so the right-hand columns sit up to about half a row higher than the row labels; figures were assigned by counting within each column block. Columns end at different months as printed: Wholesale Sept. 1939, Retail Oct. 1939, Cost of Living Aug. 1939, Labour July 1939, Production June 1939; later cells are empty (\"\"). Cost of Living has no figures for 1931-1937 annual rows (index base July 1937).",
   "Unreadable: 1935, Retail Price Index — last digit '15?' (2 or 7): '[?]'.",
   "Unreadable: 1939 June, Wholesale Consumers' goods — middle digit of '20?.4' damaged: '[?]'.",
   "1938 Dec., Rates of wages printed '87,8' (comma for decimal point), recorded as 87.8.",
   "Year labels 1932-1938 printed with ditto marks ( \" ) under '(Average)'.",
   "No printed totals; no reconciliation checks applicable."
  ],
